From: Majid Arasskhani <M.Arasskhani@gosilkroad.net>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 05:54:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/19] fix(chat): hand back the permit and the hold when turn
 preparation fails
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

build_turn_context takes the Code Interpreter permit and the budget hold
from preflight and hands them to the streaming loop, which settles them in
its finally. Only the two augmentation blocks in between released them on
failure: a raise anywhere else — building the provider kwargs, the Auto
Router probe, the workspace inventory, the persister — left the permit held
until its TTL (one concurrency slot gone) and the hold stuck.

The whole preparation is guarded now. abandon() became idempotent so the
outer guard cannot release a permit an inner handler already returned, which
would free a slot another turn is holding.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
